{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/employment-tribunal-decisions/r-l-dumitrescu-v-sopar-so-good-ltd-6007583-slash-2026","content_id":"22b0159d-9b6f-40c5-acf7-5b6b8f274090","description":"Employment Tribunal decision.","details":{"attachments":[{"attachment_type":"file","content_id":"d1df7b00-fac4-42d8-8c90-028d52ca0cdf","content_type":"application/pdf","created_at":"2026-10-01T15:52:08+01:00","id":"d1df7b00-fac4-42d8-8c90-028d52ca0cdf","title":"R L Dumitrescu v Sopar So Good Ltd: 6007583/2026 - Partial Strike Out","updated_at":"2026-10-01T15:52:08+01:00","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6abe7398f04a15f53372289f/R_L_Dumitrescu_v_SOPAR_SO_GOOD_LTD_Judgment_2__6007583-2026.pdf"}],"body":"<p>Read the full decision in <span id=\"attachment_d1df7b00-fac4-42d8-8c90-028d52ca0cdf\" class=\"attachment-inline\"><a href=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6abe7398f04a15f53372289f/R_L_Dumitrescu_v_SOPAR_SO_GOOD_LTD_Judgment_2__6007583-2026.pdf\">R L Dumitrescu v Sopar So Good Ltd: 6007583/2026 - Partial Strike Out</a></span>.</p>\n","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:29:49Z"}],"max_cache_time":10,"metadata":{"hidden_indexable_content":"each\r\nCase Number: 6007583/2026\r\nEMPLOYMENT TRIBUNALS\r\nClaimant: Radu Leonard Dumitrescu\r\nRespondent: SOPAR SO GOOD LTD\r\nJUDGMENT\r\nThe complaints of (1) unfair dismissal and (2) for a statutory redundancy payment are\r\nstruck out.\r\nREASONS\r\n1. Section 108 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 requires a claimant to have not\r\nless than two years’ service to make an unfair dismissal complaint, subject to\r\ncertain exceptions that do not appear to apply in this case.\r\n2. Section 155 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 requires a claimant to have not\r\nless than two years’ service to have an entitlement to a statutory redundancy\r\npayment.\r\n3. The claimant was employed by the respondent for less than two years. Therefore,\r\non the face of the claim, the claimant is not entitled to bring the above complaints.\r\n4. A warning letter was sent on 11 March 2026 pointing out the claimant’s lack of two\r\nyears’ continuous service. No response was received. The claimant has thus failed\r\nto give an acceptable reason, despite being given the opportunity to do so, why\r\nthe complaints subject to the two year qualifying period should not be struck out.\r\n5. Accordingly, the complaints of (1) unfair dismissal and (2) for a statutory\r\nredundancy payment are struck out. The claimant’s other complaints (notice pay,\r\nholiday pay) are not affected by this judgment.\r\nApproved by:\r\nEmployment Judge Abbott\r\nDate: 21 September 2026\r\nJUDGMENT SENT TO THE PARTIES ON\r\n28 September 2026\r\nFOR THE TRIBUNAL OFFICE\r\nP Wing","tribunal_decision_categories":["redundancy","unfair-dismissal"],"tribunal_decision_country":"england-and-wales","tribunal_decision_decision_date":"2026-09-21"},"temporary_update_type":false},"document_type":"employment_tribunal_decision","first_published_at":"2026-10-02T16:29:49+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/employment-tribunal-decisions/r-l-dumitrescu-v-sopar-so-good-ltd-6007583-slash-2026","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/employment-tribunal-decisions/r-l-dumitrescu-v-sopar-so-good-ltd-6007583-slash-2026","base_path":"/employment-tribunal-decisions/r-l-dumitrescu-v-sopar-so-good-ltd-6007583-slash-2026","content_id":"22b0159d-9b6f-40c5-acf7-5b6b8f274090","document_type":"employment_tribunal_decision","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-10-02T15:29:49Z","schema_name":"specialist_document","title":"R L Dumitrescu v Sopar So Good Ltd: 6007583/2026","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/employment-tribunal-decisions/r-l-dumitrescu-v-sopar-so-good-ltd-6007583-slash-2026","withdrawn":false}],"finder":[{"api_path":"/api/content/employment-tribunal-decisions","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/employment-tribunal-decisions","base_path":"/em